# Extension versioning

- Increment the SemVer version for every change to the shipped browser-extension package or to the extension/daemon protocol, including non-UI behavior and security fixes.
- Do not increment it for changes confined to the daemon (without changing the shipped package or protocol), CI/workflow, tests, documentation, or other non-shipped artifacts.
- Keep `browser-extension/manifest.json` and `browser-extension/manifest.chrome.json` on the same version.
- For every shipped-package/protocol bump, update version assertions, the project version in `docs/threat-model.md`, and `RELEASE_NOTES.md` in the same change.
- Run the relevant tests and `tools/build_extension.py`, then report the resulting version and artifact paths.
